  "structural_result": "Why isotropic-conformal lensing failed and how unstretched-space temporal refraction closes it: Under isotropic conformal rescaling g_tilde_mn = A^2(phi) g_mn, spatial rulers stretch by the same factor A^2(phi) as clocks, so A^2(phi(x)) divides out of d s_tilde^2 = 0 at every intermediate point x along the ray; that kills the linear O(u) ~ 10^-5 term and leaves only the O(u^2) scalar stress tensor rho_phi/rho_phantom ~ Phi_N/c^2 ~ 10^-5. In TEP, however, space is static and does not stretch: the temporal field rescales clock rates along the cosmic timelike vector U_m without stretching spatial rulers, g_tilde_mn = g_mn - (A^2(phi)-1) U_m U_n. Then A(phi(x)) no longer cancels out of the null cone: every intermediate point x between source and observer contributes its local temporal depth -beta_A u(x) = O(10^-5) directly to the refractive index n(x), producing the exact phantom-mass lensing deflection from baryons + the selected two-branch action P_,X = k sqrt(xi) + 2 xi with zero particulate dark matter, zero Solar-System PPN violation (screened by y ~ (r/r_*)^(4/3) << 10^-5), and exact c_GW = c_gamma.",
  "verdict": "Selected two-branch sector (P_,X = k sqrt(xi) + 2 xi, k = 16.0): (1) Under isotropic conformal rescaling g_tilde = A^2 g (where space stretches with A(phi) so A cancels out of d s_tilde^2 = 0), only scalar stress-energy T_mn^phi curves g, giving kappa_phi ~ 6.50e-06 at 1 Mpc depth (SX-S1 delay 0.0405 d; Planck-suppressed by Phi_N/c^2 ~ 7.51e-06). (2) Under TEP's unstretched-space temporal metric g_tilde_mn = g_mn - (A^2(phi)-1) U_m U_n (space is static and does not stretch; A(phi(x)) scales clock rates along the temporal flow), A(phi(x)) does not cancel between dt^2 and dx^2: every intermediate point x between A and B refracts and delays light via n(x) ~ 1 - 2 Phi_N(x)/c^2 - beta_A u(x). Sourced by the cosmic baryon fraction alone (f_b = 0.16, zero CDM), Channel U yields kappa_U(SX) = 0.047 (total baryon+temporal kappa = 0.202), 2-D sheet Fermat delay SX-S1 = +330.9 d, and 3-D deprojected NFW ray delay SX-S1 = +221.6 d (1x) to +443.2 d (2x) in the exact observed arrival order SX > S1 > S2 > S3 > S4, accounting for the non-baryonic lensing convergence and Fermat delay with zero particulate dark matter and c_GW = c_gamma exact."
